{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
    "name": "SwiftEats API",
    "description": "SwiftEats food delivery platform — API verification, E2E happy path, and SLO/latency checks.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start stack: `docker compose up --build` (copy `.env.example` → `.env`)\n2. Import `SwiftEats-Local.postman_environment.json` and select **SwiftEats — Local (Docker)**\n3. Run folder **01 — E2E Happy Path** with Collection Runner (1 iteration, no delay)\n\n**SLO thresholds** (environment variables):\n- `menuSloMs` = 200 (Assignment 1 menu P99 target; single-request smoke)\n- `orderCreateSloMs` = 500\n- `trackingSloMs` = 300\n\n**Metrics:** Each request logs `[METRIC] name: Xms` to the Postman console. Use Collection Runner summary for aggregate timing.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const rt = pm.response.responseTime;",
          "const name = pm.info.requestName || 'request';",
          "console.log(`[METRIC] ${name}: ${rt}ms status=${pm.response.code}`);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastResponseTimeMs', String(rt));",
          "",
          "pm.test('Response received', function () {",
          "    pm.response.to.not.be.error;",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "lastResponseTimeMs", "value": "" },
    { "key": "menuLatencySamples", "value": "[]" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — E2E Happy Path",
      "description": "Run this folder top-to-bottom in Collection Runner after docker-compose is healthy. Re-run **04 — Get order (poll payment)** if status is still PENDING_PAYMENT.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 — Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Health is UP', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "02 — List restaurants (Pune)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/restaurants?city=Pune&page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "restaurants"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "city", "value": "Pune" },
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Returns restaurant page', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().content).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "03 — Get menu (SLO smoke)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const slo = parseInt(pm.environment.get('menuSloMs') || '200', 10);",
                  "pm.test('Menu returns 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(`Menu latency < ${slo}ms (A1 smoke)`, function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(slo);",
                  "});",
                  "let samples = [];",
                  "try { samples = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('menuLatencySamples') || '[]'); } catch (e) {}",
                  "samples.push(pm.response.responseTime);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('menuLatencySamples', JSON.stringify(samples));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "04 — Create order",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.environment.set('idempotencyKey', 'postman-e2e-' + Date.now());"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const slo = parseInt(pm.environment.get('orderCreateSloMs') || '500', 10);",
                  "pm.test('Order accepted 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(`Create order latency < ${slo}ms`, function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(slo);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('orderId returned', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.orderId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('orderId', body.orderId);",
                  "console.log('[E2E] orderId=' + body.orderId);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Idempotency-Key", "value": "{{idempotencyKey}}" },
              { "key": "X-Customer-Id", "value": "{{customerId}}" },
              { "key": "X-Customer-Api-Key", "value": "{{customerApiToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"restaurantId\": \"{{restaurantId}}\",\n  \"deliveryAddress\": \"123 MG Road, Pune\",\n  \"city\": \"Pune\",\n  \"state\": \"Maharashtra\",\n  \"pincode\": \"411001\",\n  \"paymentMode\": \"UPI\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"menuItemId\": \"{{menuItemId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 2\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "05 — Get order (poll payment)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Customer-Id", "value": "{{customerId}}" },
              { "key": "X-Customer-Api-Key", "value": "{{customerApiToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Order readable', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const status = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "console.log('[E2E] order status=' + status);",
                  "if (status === 'CONFIRMED' || status === 'PREPARING' || status === 'OUT_FOR_DELIVERY' || status === 'DELIVERED') {",
                  "    pm.test('Payment progressed beyond PENDING_PAYMENT', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(status).to.not.eql('PENDING_PAYMENT');",
                  "    });",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn('Payment still processing — wait 2s and re-run this request');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "06 — Admin: PREPARING",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Admin-Api-Key", "value": "{{adminApiKey}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"PREPARING\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"postman-kitchen\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/state"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Transition to PREPARING', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('PREPARING');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "07 — Admin: OUT_FOR_DELIVERY",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Admin-Api-Key", "value": "{{adminApiKey}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"OUT_FOR_DELIVERY\",\n  \"changedBy\": \"postman-kitchen\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/state"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Transition to OUT_FOR_DELIVERY + driver assigned', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('OUT_FOR_DELIVERY');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.driverId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "08 — Post driver GPS",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Driver-Api-Key", "value": "{{driverApiToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"latitude\": 18.5204,\n  \"longitude\": 73.8567,\n  \"heading\": 135,\n  \"orderId\": \"{{orderId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drivers/{{driverId}}/location"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('GPS accepted 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "09 — Get tracking snapshot (SLO smoke)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Customer-Id", "value": "{{customerId}}" },
              { "key": "X-Customer-Api-Key", "value": "{{customerApiToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/tracking"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const slo = parseInt(pm.environment.get('trackingSloMs') || '300', 10);",
                  "pm.test('Tracking snapshot 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().latitude).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(`Tracking latency < ${slo}ms`, function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(slo);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "10 — Get order history",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Customer-Id", "value": "{{customerId}}" },
              { "key": "X-Customer-Api-Key", "value": "{{customerApiToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/history"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('History is non-empty array', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — Metrics / Menu burst",
      "description": "Run this folder with Collection Runner (10–20 iterations) to approximate menu read latency distribution. Check console for `[METRIC]` lines; export runner results for p95/p99 offline.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Menu burst (single iteration)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const slo = parseInt(pm.environment.get('menuSloMs') || '200', 10);",
                  "pm.test('Menu 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(`Latency < ${slo}ms`, function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(slo);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — Restaurants (public)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List restaurants",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/restaurants?city=Pune",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "restaurants"],
              "query": [{ "key": "city", "value": "Pune" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get restaurant menu",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 — Orders (customer auth)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create order",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.environment.set('idempotencyKey', 'postman-' + Date.now());"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 202) {",
